  <h2>The goGreenlit Testing Approach</h2>
  <p>Most outsourced testing operates outside the development process. Tickets go in, results come back, and nobody is quite sure what got tested. We built goGreenlit specifically to not work that way.</p>
  <p>We start from a shift-left model: quality checks happen earlier in the cycle, before the cost of fixing problems escalates. That means participating in sprint planning to identify testing scope, writing test cases before implementation starts, and running smoke tests on pull requests before they merge to main.</p>
  <p>Sprint-embedded means we are in your standup, your retrospective, and your defect triage. You know what we tested. You know what we found. You know what is in the backlog. There are no surprises at release time.</p>
  <p>Coverage-driven means we track metrics over time. Not lines of code covered by automated tests – that number is nearly meaningless in isolation. We track functional coverage: what percentage of your defined test cases were executed, what percentage passed, and what escaped to production despite test coverage. Those numbers tell you something real.</p>

  <h2>Technologies We Cover</h2>
  <p>We work across the modern web and mobile stack. On the frontend: React, Next.js, Vue, Angular, and server-rendered applications. On the backend: Node.js, Python, Java, and Go APIs. For databases: PostgreSQL, MySQL, MongoDB, and Redis. For infrastructure: AWS, GCP, and Azure environments.</p>
  <p>For test tooling: Playwright, Selenium WebDriver, Postman, REST Assured, PyTest, Cypress (migration assessment), and Appium for mobile. For CI/CD: GitHub Actions, Jenkins, GitLab CI, and CircleCI.</p>
  <p>If your stack isn't on this list, ask. We have enough breadth to adapt to most environments.</p>

